text.section:
Any permanent splice or repair in a trailing cable shall:

Be mechanically strong, with adequate electrical conductivity and flexibility;


Be effectively insulated and sealed so as to exclude moisture;


Be vulcanized or otherwise treated with suitable materials to provide flame-resistant properties and good bonding to the outer jacket; and


If the cable has metallic shielding around each conductor, possess new shielding that is equivalent to the original shielding.
